course: dictionary
lesson: 1690
title: Chronicle: events in order
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A chronicle is a written record of events in the order they happened. The word events is your first clue, and the words in order are the second. «The Primary Chronicle was put together around 1113» tells you that the writer recorded things in time order, from earlier to later.
explain: Chronicle comes from the Greek word chronos, which means time. That is why a chronicle puts things in the order they happened, and why the verb to chronicle means to record events in order. Try your meaning in the sentence: «Moscow is first mentioned in a chronicle in 1147» makes sense if chronicle means a written record of events.
explain: The same word is also used for newspapers and story series, such as «The Chronicles of Narnia». Here it is a name, so look at the words around it. A name in a title is not a list of events, so you must read the context to see which meaning fits.
explain: Historians do not believe every chronicle word for word. «It mixes facts and legends, so historians check it against archaeology and foreign sources.» When you read a chronicle, ask: is this fact, or is it a story that people told?
fact: A chronicle is a written record of events in the order they happened.
fact: To chronicle means to record events in order.
fact: Chronicle comes from the Greek word chronos, which means time.
fact: Chronicles can also be newspapers or story series, such as «The Chronicles of Narnia».
fact: The Primary Chronicle, also called the Tale of Bygone Years, was put together around 1113.
fact: Chronicles can mix facts and legends, so historians check them against other evidence.
exercise: «Moscow is first mentioned in a chronicle in 1147.» In this sentence, what does chronicle mean? | A cold drink | *A written record of events in time order | A sort of game | A kind of small boat
exercise: Nadia says chronicle only means a newspaper. What is missing from her idea? | *It also means to record events in order, and a written record of events in order | Newspapers never record anything | Chronicles are always short | It means a kind of food
exercise: «The Chronicles of Narnia» is a famous book series. In this title, what does Chronicles mean? | *A series of stories | A type of weather | A map of the sea | Words to say hello
test: «The Primary Chronicle was put together around 1113, probably at the Kyiv Caves Monastery.» Where was it probably put together? | In Moscow | At a school in London | *At the Kyiv Caves Monastery | On a ship at sea
test: Why do historians check a chronicle against archaeology and foreign sources? | Because chronicles are too short to read | Because archaeology is a kind of story | *Because chronicles can mix facts and legends | Because chronicles are always wrong
exam: Chronicle comes from the Greek word chronos. What does chronos mean? | *Time | Stone | Sleep | Water
